  "note": "First election of the new urban district council of Newtownabbey, 21 members for seven wards (three each), polling 21 May 1958. Carnmoney, Cavehill and Glengormley were uncontested; the results of the other four wards were declared on 22 and 23 May. Percentage poll 63; total electorate 2,284; one spoiled vote."
